Phase 2: Login and Logout
Implement login and logout functionality.
Requirements:
3
• Users must be able to log in using their username and password.
• Verify the submitted password against the stored password hash.
• Create a server-side Session after successful login.
• Store the user's ID and username in the Session.
• Display the logged-in user's username on the main page.
• The user must remain logged in while the Session is valid in the same browser.
• When the user logs out, invalidate the Session.
Endpoints:
Method Endpoint Description
POST /login Log in
POST /logout Log out

Phase 3: Adding and Viewing Books

Implement functionality for adding and viewing books. Only logged-in users can add books.
Endpoints:
• POST /api/books — Add a book
• GET /api/books — Get all books
Use Java record types for DTOs and return book information as JSON.

Phase 4: Updating and Deleting Books

Implement functionality for updating and deleting a specific book using its ID.
Endpoints:
• PUT /api/books/{id} — Update a book
• DELETE /api/books/{id} — Delete a book
If the specified book does not exist, return an appropriate response.

Phase 5: Filters, Cookies, and Frontend

Part A: Filters
• Implement an Encoding Filter to set the character encoding to UTF-8.
• Implement a Logging Filter that logs messages before and after each request.
• Configure the Filters in web.xml to demonstrate Filter Chaining and execution order.

Part B: Cookies
After login, create a Cookie containing the username.
Endpoint: GET /api/username
Read the username from the Cookie and return it as JSON. Do not read it from the Session or
request parameters.

Part C: Frontend
Create a simple HTML page to manage books.
• Use Fetch API to communicate with the backend.
• Use JavaScript event listeners to handle user actions.
• Display the list of books and the results of adding, updating, and deleting books.